From 70c4871a4d16e26b46c27c56e19e9b105ffbb0d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:11:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [d3d11] narrow typeless colour textures to their UNORM view
 formats

Typeless RGBA8 and RGB10A2 textures that only D3D11 sees get just their UNORM (and sRGB) view formats, so that drivers such as Turnip on the Adreno 6xx keep them compressed. A view in another format of the family before the texture's first use rebuilds it with the whole family and copies its contents; a later one logs a warning (d3d11.narrowTypelessFormats, on by default).
